  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of MONGODB SHARDING. Your shard key is the one decision MongoDB will not let you take back cheaply, and most teams pick it from the field that felt like the natural primary key. This handbook walks the full chain: cluster anatomy, how keys turn documents into chunks, ranged vs hashed, why a missing key turns every read into a scatter-gather, and what the balancer is actually doing while your p99 spikes. Ends with the decision framework and the repair commands you hope you never need.",
